{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350878-thoughts-on-integrating-scion-and-trinity","id":1350878,"title":"Thoughts on integrating Scion and Trinity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-25T12:22:08-08:00","id":1350878,"title":"Thoughts on integrating Scion and Trinity","content":"I'm considering pulling stuff from Scion into my Trinity game. Has anyone else tried this and if so, what where the results? Just a cursory look at the character creation system puts me in the mind of them being near Nova level at least. Really I don't think I'll bring Scion stuff in straight up, but Scions/Titans would be pretty useful doubles for Extants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T13:51:44-08:00","id":1350902,"title":"","content":"I'd say Origin level characters are around Talents in power, and Hero is more in the psion level with more versatility. Although, a proxy level psion is probably stronger than most Heroes. Scion: Hero doesn't use the Scale system as much as Aberrant does. So, give yourself Scale 2 or higher, and you'll be well over a Hero in whatever area you have that Scale in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T13:59:01-08:00","id":1350903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350878-thoughts-on-integrating-scion-and-trinity?p=1350902#post1350902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say Origin level characters are around Talents in power, and Hero is more in the psion level with more versatility. Although, a proxy level psion is probably stronger than most Heroes. Scion: Hero doesn't use the Scale system as much as Aberrant does. So, give yourself Scale 2 or higher, and you'll be well over a Hero in whatever area you have that Scale in.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are grossly underestimating Talents. Talents are Tier 2 characters on par with Psions, Psiads, and Superiors. Their incredible power just plays out more extra diagetically, but Origin level Scions don\u2019t come close to the full might of Dramatic Editing and the ability to seize emergency Scale at will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T14:05:26-08:00","id":1350907,"title":"","content":"The aesthetics and settings are very different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T15:42:56-08:00","id":1350917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350878-thoughts-on-integrating-scion-and-trinity?p=1350903#post1350903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are grossly underestimating Talents. Talents are Tier 2 characters on par with Psions, Psiads, and Superiors. Their incredible power just plays out more extra diagetically, but Origin level Scions don\u2019t come close to the full might of Dramatic Editing and the ability to seize emergency Scale at will.</div> </div> </div> </div>At base character creation, Scions hold the advantage with Skills. An Origin Scion and a Hero Scion each get 23 dots to spend in skills. However, they don't get anything for Edges because edges aren't really a thing in Scion. So, figure Trinity-Scions would need to share the base character creation process of everyone else in terms of Paths, Attributes, Skills and Edges. Origin Scions then get one Knack and then either 4 points of Birthrights or two more Knacks (but can only have one active at any given time). By comparison, Talents get four Gifts as well as a point of Inspiration and three points to develop their Facets.<br /> <br /> Heroes, meanwhile, get up to 5 Heroic Knacks (or a mixture of Heroic and more potent Immortal Knacks), and get 7 points of Birthrights (which resemble some Edges but have other powers) and also get two Boons, which are pretty blatant supernatural powers.<br /> <br /> In terms of Trinity, I'd call Origin Scions about Tier 1.5 and Hero Scions Tier 2.5<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T21:02:44-08:00","id":1350966,"title":"","content":"Depends on how you are expecting to &quot;pull stuff&quot; from Scion.<br /> <br /> Using some of the powers as inspiration for new Gifts or Enhanced Edges? Should be easy.<br /> <br /> Porting over Scions wholesale as a PC type? That's a pretty tall order. Even though there is a unified underlying system, the approaches the games take to their mechanics function on very different assumptions. There's a bit of overlap when it comes to Knacks with Edges and Gifts. There's also a very different mentality when it comes to the way Legend is used and regained against how the other various power stats go in TC.<br /> <br /> Dunno if you are rpg.net averse, but there was a recent thread over there that explored this.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/storypath-mixing-scion-and-trinity.851399/\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?thre...rinity.851399/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T00:52:59-08:00","id":1350990,"title":"","content":"A few details I would change to get a cross over done (my approach is bringing Scion to TC).<br /> <br /> I would use the TC char creation for Scions, it means everybody have Edges.<br /> <br /> Callings and Knacks would become a Scion only trait, as they gain legend they gain their play is in fate game, what it represented by Callings. They keep edges and all, but the Callings and Knacks get more important to a Scion than the rest.<br /> <br /> Scion Purviews are very opened, it means lot of versatility, while most of the powers in TC are pretty straight forward. I would keep it that way, the rise of legend is much limited by the entire group and their deeds, what would compensate the fast pace TC characters can rise if they focus on a trait. I know novas can do Power stunts and all, but scions are basically walking sources of power stunts.<br /> <br /> Last but not Least, Scion TC game is meant to be short. As it was pointed, Scions grow from mortal to gods, while TC characters stop somewhere. A Psion/Scion x-over bust end by the time they rise to Demigods, otherwise the power gap will be too much, the same way a Nova/Scion must start when the Scions are closer to Demigods and will end with a bunch of gods and monsters.<br /> <br /> There is also the Relic/ Super Science correlation, but it\u2019s probably the fastest to solve, I just didn\u2019t think about it... not enough at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 11-26-2019, 03:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T05:39:52-08:00","id":1351020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350878-thoughts-on-integrating-scion-and-trinity?p=1350903#post1350903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are grossly underestimating Talents. Talents are Tier 2 characters on par with Psions, Psiads, and Superiors. Their incredible power just plays out more extra diagetically, but Origin level Scions don\u2019t come close to the full might of Dramatic Editing and the ability to seize emergency Scale at will.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. I was thinking more of how Talents and Origin level Scions have kind of similar feelings to their powers. Their powers are more generally more subtle than heroes/psions/novas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T09:11:05-08:00","id":1351054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350878-thoughts-on-integrating-scion-and-trinity?p=1351020#post1351020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True. I was thinking more of how Talents and Origin level Scions have kind of similar feelings to their powers. Their powers are more generally more subtle than heroes/psions/novas.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just getting my feet wet learning the Scion system. One interesting things about Heroes and Demigods/Gods is that their more powerful abilities cannot be purchased with XP. They can buy Knacks, Heroic and Immortal with XP. They can also buy Birthrights (creatures, followers, guides and relics) with XP. Apparently Legend (which powers their stuff, Callings, Purviews and Boons (higher powered abilities) cannot be gained through XP and must be earned another way.<br /> <br /> If I let Scions be PCs, I'll probably tweak the template a bit to make them fit into the base Tier II levels of other Aeon and Core PCs. Birthrights will become Edges (Pets/Creatures will be a version of the Old Trinity Allies Merit; Followers will be Followers; Guides will be Mentors and Relics will be Artifacts of a slightly different flavor).<br /> <br /> One thing I'll also do is reduce certain restrictions. Anybody can buy Edges unless they are specifically restricted to a specific Path or character type. Only Psions can buy their version of Enhanced Mode. Only Novas can buy Dormancy. Anybody can buy and use Artifacts and Enhanced Edges. They can't alter, repair or potentially even recharge said Artifacts, but they can use them assuming they're relatively general purpose (A &quot;norm&quot; could use a gun that fires Quantum Bolts but couldn't use a helmet that enhances Telepathy because he wouldn't have Telepathy). Do we assume that every head of state or CEO of a major corporation is a Talent, Nova or Psion/Psiad? As for Artifacts, restricted them to Novas and Psi-types closes a lot of story space. How many stories begin with the idea of a normal human person finding some weird thingie that empowers them and changes their lives for better or worse? You're telling me I can't run <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0077834/?ref_=nv_sr_srsg_0\" target=\"_blank\">Laserblast </a>in my game because the twerp picking about the weird quantum gun would need to start as a Nova? Screw that. &quot;Muggles&quot; should be just as viable as threats/dangers as powered characters. I remember from the campaign where I played the low-powered Nova that one of the most powerful characters in the game was a Neutral normal human out of Japan. He'd bought Status links to the government and a high Wealth. So, even though he had no psionic, quantum or knacks, he was cybered up the ass to the point that he almost functioned as a Biokinetic and Electrokinetic. He was kind of the poster boy for that bit from Justice League of &quot;What's your superpower?&quot; &quot;I'm rich.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm thinking of allowing Heroic Mundanes in as Tier II characters. Basically they'd go through Steps 1-4 and 6, skipping the powered template thing. After Step 6 they'd get 50 XP to buy further skills, Attributes and Edges. Should they later wish to become Inspired/Powered, they can, but they'd need to accumulate sufficient XP to pay for their empowerment as though they were being initially created as that type (figure something like 60-75 XP). They could still spend other XP, but they'd need to save a lot of it for their eventual transformation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","user":"johntfs","date":". 11-26-2019, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-11T21:21:22-08:00","id":1360447,"title":"","content":"Beyond the issues of power balance and pacing, are there any nuts-and-bolts differences (i.e., dramatic systems/underlying game engine) between the two games? I haven't done a literal side-by-side comparison with both books open in front of me, but the system looks very similar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T03:05:55-08:00","id":1360482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350878-thoughts-on-integrating-scion-and-trinity?p=1360447#post1360447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beyond the issues of power balance and pacing, are there any nuts-and-bolts differences (i.e., dramatic systems/underlying game engine) between the two games? I haven't done a literal side-by-side comparison with both books open in front of me, but the system looks very similar.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are more than a few:<br /> Scion paths have no dots, Trinity does. It impact the way you deal with contacts.<br /> On character creation paths have a much bigger impact on Scion, almost all the skill dots are locked on the paths, while Trinity is more opened.<br /> The total Skill and attributes dots from character creation are different.<br /> The way you evolve in Scion and in Trinity is different, Scion you use your XP for \u201cmortal stuff\u201d and gain real power from the Legend, that require group effort to raise, in Trinity you use XP for everything.<br /> Scion characters have a small number of Knacks, linked to their Callings. trinity characters have no Callings and have a large number of edges. The Knacks are in a certain way powerful edges, but they evolve different.<br /> the number of Injury box are different (the total is the same, but Bruised and Injured have different numbers)<br /> Many weapon and armor tags work different.<br /> The types of damage are different.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s what come to mind now. Probably there are more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T09:58:20-08:00","id":1360542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350878-thoughts-on-integrating-scion-and-trinity?p=1360482#post1360482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are more than a few:<br /> Scion paths have no dots, Trinity does. It impact the way you deal with contacts.<br /> On character creation paths have a much bigger impact on Scion, almost all the skill dots are locked on the paths, while Trinity is more opened.<br /> The total Skill and attributes dots from character creation are different.<br /> The way you evolve in Scion and in Trinity is different, Scion you use your XP for \u201cmortal stuff\u201d and gain real power from the Legend, that require group effort to raise, in Trinity you use XP for everything.<br /> Scion characters have a small number of Knacks, linked to their Callings. trinity characters have no Callings and have a large number of edges. The Knacks are in a certain way powerful edges, but they evolve different.<br /> the number of Injury box are different (the total is the same, but Bruised and Injured have different numbers)<br /> Many weapon and armor tags work different.<br /> The types of damage are different.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s what come to mind now. Probably there are more.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While the Knacks can be &quot;powerful Edges&quot; they are supernatural/powered in nature. Scion is the older version of the Storypath system and it's less tethered to &quot;the real world.&quot; That said, with a little work, it wouldn't be too hard to convert Scion to Trinity. Birthrights would be Artifacts, of a sort. Edges would work normally. Figure Origin and Hero Scions would be Tier II, while Demigod and God would be Tier III and Tier IV respectively.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T12:12:09-08:00","id":1360565,"title":"","content":"I would absolutely take the different skill for each range band chart from Scion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T17:20:32-08:00","id":1360612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werlynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350878-thoughts-on-integrating-scion-and-trinity?p=1360565#post1360565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would absolutely take the different skill for each range band chart from Scion</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s the same skill but different Attributes. And it was the same for Trinity, except it was taken away to avoid confusion. I think it is one of the great ideas in Storypath, not only for tang band changes, but for some different weapons different attributes can be used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T17:37:05-08:00","id":1360614,"title":"","content":"My bad. Yeah I love it. It assumes if you\u2019re in close you\u2019re wrestling with the gun, but if you\u2019re medium range then you\u2019re out-thinking a moving target. It makes a gunslinger or sniper more diverse than a one-attribute pony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T05:55:19-08:00","id":1360680,"title":"","content":"Specialties work differently as well. In TC, they add a halo bonus to other skills, in Scion you get extra momentum if you fail a roll with a skill you have a specialty in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T23:20:08-08:00","id":1361220,"title":"","content":"I admit, the idea of Trinity: PScion amuses me, just for the pun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T12:29:46-08:00","id":1362193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350878-thoughts-on-integrating-scion-and-trinity?p=1360680#post1360680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Specialties work differently as well. In TC, they add a halo bonus to other skills, in Scion you get extra momentum if you fail a roll with a skill you have a specialty in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feels like Scion pays out more for Momentum turn around. Right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1472-mostlyjoe","name":"Mostlyjoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1472_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T05:27:23-08:00","id":1362377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mostlyjoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350878-thoughts-on-integrating-scion-and-trinity?p=1362193#post1362193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Feels like Scion pays out more for Momentum turn around. Right?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's the only difference I can think of regarding Momentum generation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T06:10:11-08:00","id":1362625,"title":"","content":"Another thing I\u2019d bring from Scion is a recommended cap on enhancements from outside of powers. At the very least a GM recommendation to consider a sort of soft diminishing returns rather than stacking up 8+ enhancements at a time. I know it\u2019s built into \u00c6on psi powers to have super high enhancements instead of applying scale, so leave that alone. If you\u2019re running core be mindful of how high enhancements stack. I don\u2019t see the same warning box that Scion has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T06:18:08-08:00","id":1362627,"title":"","content":"My house rule for Enhancement stacks is:<br /> Max 3 if only a bunch of +1<br /> Max 4 if there is at least one +2<br /> Max 5 if there is at least one +3<br /> Except for scale, there is no single enhancement higher than 3.<br /> Psi powers that grants enhancement 4 instead grant +2 and 1 scale and if grants 5 instead grants +3 and 1 scale<br /> <br /> I am quite sure they removed the hard cap on +5, except for the content on Aberrant Maniscript.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T06:19:04-08:00","id":1362629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werlynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350878-thoughts-on-integrating-scion-and-trinity?p=1362625#post1362625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing I\u2019d bring from Scion is a recommended cap on enhancements from outside of powers. At the very least a GM recommendation to consider a sort of soft diminishing returns rather than stacking up 8+ enhancements at a time. I know it\u2019s built into \u00c6on psi powers to have super high enhancements instead of applying scale, so leave that alone. If you\u2019re running core be mindful of how high enhancements stack. I don\u2019t see the same warning box that Scion has.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do have to be a little careful here. If a group of psions is going up against a Terat, they may need to build up some teamwork/feint enhancements to be able to overcome a Terat's defense and armor. In one battle, the group was passing around 4 or 5 enhancements to melee attacks in order to injure the Nemesis they were fighting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T09:49:21-08:00","id":1362669,"title":"","content":"Their mortal, human scale abilities <i>shouldn\u2019t</i> be able to just stack up to defeat a terat. No amount of feinting and teamwork will help you break a car or a tank with your kung fu. Powerful aberrants are tanks. That\u2019s scale. They build things or do things that change their scale and that balance the playing field. They build a VARG that raises their scale. They use an anti-particle asteroid mining laser that is meant to bore through thinks with the toughness of space rocks. I specifically said I wouldn\u2019t limit the enhancement bonus of psi powers, but everything else about both psions and talents is baseline mortal, human scale. Tier is not directly part of scale. Even the proxies are human scale if the can\u2019t manage to bring their powers to the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T10:32:55-08:00","id":1362676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350878-thoughts-on-integrating-scion-and-trinity?p=1362627#post1362627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My house rule for Enhancement stacks is:<br /> Max 3 if only a bunch of +1<br /> Max 4 if there is at least one +2<br /> Max 5 if there is at least one +3<br /> Except for scale, there is no single enhancement higher than 3.<br /> Psi powers that grants enhancement 4 instead grant +2 and 1 scale and if grants 5 instead grants +3 and 1 scale<br /> <br /> I am quite sure they removed the hard cap on +5, except for the content on Aberrant Maniscript.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You might want to consider working through some of the many sources of Enhancement on Psi powers, and work out where switching to Scale might be a good idea. Bunyip has commented before that the amount of enhancement that Psions get was intentional, and if it was going to be capped there would need to be adjustments.<br /> <br /> As is, it is very easy to get very high enhancement without min maxing. A three dot thermokinetic with Strong Mode has +6 enhancement (3 from the power itself, 1 from having a mode rating higher than the power, and 2 from strong mode). This is before linking up with any of the aptitudes that provide additional enhancement, or just having a higher dot rating. Would also make Dysfunction, well, dysfunctional, as it would almost immediately bump into that cap.<br /> <br /> There had been some talk of an optional rule where psions would have a stunt to turn excess enhancement into increased scale, but it wasn't in the \u00c6xpansion and we haven't heard anything else about it. My guess is that it will pop up in the final Aberrant text next to the Edge that lets Talents compete, but that is just my wild speculation.<br /> <br /> edit: failed my crtical reading roll where you suggested enhancements of 4 grant 2 and 1 scale. leaving post for posterity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T11:05:23-08:00","id":1362684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werlynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350878-thoughts-on-integrating-scion-and-trinity?p=1362669#post1362669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their mortal, human scale abilities <i>shouldn\u2019t</i> be able to just stack up to defeat a terat. No amount of feinting and teamwork will help you break a car or a tank with your kung fu. Powerful aberrants are tanks. That\u2019s scale. They build things or do things that change their scale and that balance the playing field. They build a VARG that raises their scale. They use an anti-particle asteroid mining laser that is meant to bore through thinks with the toughness of space rocks. I specifically said I wouldn\u2019t limit the enhancement bonus of psi powers, but everything else about both psions and talents is baseline mortal, human scale. Tier is not directly part of scale. Even the proxies are human scale if the can\u2019t manage to bring their powers to the situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are plenty of examples in media of a group working together to distract and maneuver a normally invincible opponent to expose their weak spot to someone on the team in order to injure them. There's also plenty of examples in media of someone like Black Widow taking out something of the power level of The Hulk with nothing but skill. Unless you're packing enough scale into a terat's armor/defense/durability to put them 4 scale above the PCs (which without mutations or qualities would use up most to all of a terat's scale) the PCs should be able to damage a terat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T16:09:11-08:00","id":1362747,"title":"","content":"The Skills need to be standardized. Firearms as Aim only works until the Deva show up and want to use a bow with Athletics because that is their Pantheon Path.<br /> <br /> The Scale chart is slightly different between the two games (off by one in direct comparisons). When directly importing antagonists, update their stats accordingly.<br /> <br /> Followers appear on both the Edge and Birthright lists and work the same way, which is an issue. That said, Birthrights have been hinted at growing in power as you rise in tier so...<br /> <br /> The interaction between the Wealth edge and the Prosperity Purview needs to be considered if not addressed.<br /> <br /> Crafting has minor differences, but it is easy saying baselines and Inspired can't make magic items above tier one and Legendary beings can only venture as far as Advanced Science (not Inspired or Powered).<br /> <br /> Scions and Denizens can generate their own Scale with their Titles and Deeds. While this won't be a common occurrence, it does mean they can overcome obstacles unexpectedly compared to Trinity characters of the same tier.<br /> <br /> As for the concerns about the limited shelf life of Scion before they ascend, I'd argue you could just not let them move up a tier until it is less of an issue. By all means, give them the exp for completing deeds but Legend basically goes up via Fiat anyway. There is not a lot of 'sideways' growth in Scion but Edges and the ability to purchase hew Paths in Trinity would help a lot with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T16:38:15-08:00","id":1362755,"title":"","content":"The thing about scale and powers in Scion and Trinity is not about the frequency but about flexibility.<br /> <br /> Scion is flexible, basically if it\u2019s sounds good it works as desired, because that\u2019s how myths work. Booms, miracles and uses of titles are ABSOLUTELY flexible, just pick the proper point of view or motif and Bang, it works. Novas CAN do that as power stunts... well, novas can do anything... but they are on Demigod Tier, so it\u2019s expected from them.<br /> <br /> Psions in the other hand, are very focused on their powers, it\u2019s not like they are completely restrained, but they can\u2019t go too far away from the center point, even combining modes. Talents are flexible in the dramatic edition, more restricted by the gifts, but they lack the scale capacities of heroes, at least comparing to L3-4 heroes.<br /> <br /> Honestly I really want to see what Ian and the devs will bring in Aegis, it\u2019s probably the closest we are going to get from a cross over...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T19:03:02-08:00","id":1362778,"title":"","content":"I know for me I am thinking the other way round. Scion seems to be missing a lot. Though I do understand some design philosophies Neil was going for with Scion however for me as a story guid and my players wanting a higher granularity to their characters. Around my gaming table we all miss the finer details for controlling character wealth, fame and a many of the small things it feels like Trinity has on lock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T07:11:52-08:00","id":1362876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350878-thoughts-on-integrating-scion-and-trinity?p=1362684#post1362684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are plenty of examples in media of a group working together to distract and maneuver a normally invincible opponent to expose their weak spot to someone on the team in order to injure them. There's also plenty of examples in media of someone like Black Widow taking out something of the power level of The Hulk with nothing but skill. Unless you're packing enough scale into a terat's armor/defense/durability to put them 4 scale above the PCs (which without mutations or qualities would use up most to all of a terat's scale) the PCs should be able to damage a terat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you suggesting that Black Widow is not a Talent with the gift \u201cThe Bigger They Are\u201d (think I got the name right) from the Aberrant book? Because that\u2019s absolutely what she is if you translate her to this setting. I also challenge your implication that she does it by fighting on their terms. She\u2019d either use tech or change the situation to one where their scale doesn\u2019t apply, or just not \u201cattack\u201d with the method they have scale to defend against. None of that is just stacking 8 levels of enhancement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T11:23:15-08:00","id":1362918,"title":"","content":"No. I'm suggesting there should be more ways for PCs to deal with a Terat than to use their psi powers or equipment to gain scale. It looks to me like we're just arguing from the perspective of two different play styles. Thankfully, the rules allow us to each run it the way we want, since I can always just make sure any NPC's durability scale doesn't get too high.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T15:18:43-08:00","id":1362965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350878-thoughts-on-integrating-scion-and-trinity?p=1362918#post1362918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It looks to me like we're just arguing from the perspective of two different play styles. Thankfully, the rules allow us to each run it the way we want, since I can always just make sure any NPC's durability scale doesn't get too high.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely \ud83d\udc4d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}